<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="palabras-ws-letsReadTagalog" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Let's Read Tagalog! (<em>Magbasa tayo ng Tagalog!</em>)</title>
  
  <page>
    <p>We translated <alert>20</alert> phrases from English to Tagalog. We have the two lists below, but they are not in the same order!</p>
    
<sidebyside widths="50% 46%" margins="0% 0%" valign="top">
          <tabular>
  <col width="48%"/>
  <col halign="center"/>
  <row header="yes" bottom="major"><cell>English word/phrase</cell><cell>len</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Tea</p></cell><cell>3</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>tiger</p></cell><cell>5</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>a bear</p></cell><cell>5</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>elephant</p></cell><cell>8</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>crazy shark</p></cell><cell>10</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>a purple owl</p></cell><cell>10</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>a black dolphin</p></cell><cell>13</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p><alert>The pink panther</alert></p></cell><cell>14</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Reading is exciting</p></cell><cell>17</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Better late than never</p></cell><cell>19</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Out of sight, out of mind</p></cell><cell>20</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>The proof is in the pudding</p></cell><cell>22</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Don't cry over spilled milk</p></cell><cell>23</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Don't eat the green apples yet</p></cell><cell>25</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Laughter is the best medicine</p></cell><cell>25</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Don't judge a book by its cover</p></cell><cell>25</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>The early bird catches the worm</p></cell><cell>26</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Dance like nobody's watching you</p></cell><cell>28</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>A picture is worth a thousand words</p></cell><cell>29</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Time flies when you are reading books</p></cell><cell>31</cell></row>
</tabular>

<tabular>
  <col width="60%"/>
  <col halign="center"/>
  <row header="yes" bottom="major"><cell>Tagalog word/phrase</cell><cell>len</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Tsaa</p></cell><cell>4</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Tigre</p></cell><cell>5</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Isang oso</p></cell><cell>8</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Elepante</p></cell><cell>8</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Mabaliw na pating</p></cell><cell>15</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Isang lila na kuwago</p></cell><cell>17</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p><alert>Ang rosas na pantera</alert></p></cell><cell>17</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Isang itim na dolphin</p></cell><cell>18</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Mas mabuti nang huli kaysa wala</p></cell><cell>26</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Huwag umiyak sa nabasang gatas</p></cell><cell>26</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Ang patunay ay nasa kinalabasan</p></cell><cell>27</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Ang pagbabasa ay kapana-panabik</p></cell><cell>28</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Pag wala sa paningin, wala sa isip</p></cell><cell>28</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Ang tawanan ay pinakamagandang gamot</p></cell><cell>32</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Ang maagap ay nakakakuha ng pagkakataon</p></cell><cell>34</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Sumayaw ka parang walang nanonood sa'yo</p></cell><cell>35</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Huwag mong kainin ang mga berdeng mansanas</p></cell><cell>36</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Huwag husgahan ang aklat sa kanyang pabalat</p></cell><cell>37</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Mabilis ang oras kapag nagbabasa ka ng mga aklat</p></cell><cell>40</cell></row>
  <row bottom="minor"><cell><p>Isang larawan ay mas makapangyarihan kaysa libong salita</p></cell><cell>49</cell></row>
</tabular>
        </sidebyside>
   
    <exercise xml:id="ex-tagalog-grow">
      <statement>
        <p>Look at the two lists. In general, do you think that the number of letters is larger in ENG or TAG?<fillin characters="10"/></p>
      </statement>
      <solution>
        <p>Increase (looking at the lists).</p>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
  </page>
    
    <p>Using the correct matching, someone created the following graph to relate the 20 phrases in the lists. Each point represents a pair of corresponding phrases from the two languages.</p>

    <!-- <image source="palabras-tagalog-graph.png" width="80%"/> -->
    <image margins="0%">
      <shortdescription>A scatter plot titled "Comparing lengths of phrases English (ENG) Vs. Tagalog (TAG)", with the length of the phrase in English on the horizontal axis (0 to 50) and the length of the phrase in Tagalog on the vertical axis (0 to 50). Twenty points rise roughly along a line, with one point around (29, 49) standing above the others.</shortdescription>
      <latex-image>
        <xi:include parse="text" href="tikz/palabras-graph.tex"/>
      </latex-image>
    </image>
<page>
    <exercise xml:id="ex-tagalog-point" workspace="1cm">
      <statement>
        

        <p>What information can we get from each point of the graph? Give an example.</p>

      </statement>
      <solution>
        <p>It gives us the relationship between the length of phrases in the two languages. For example, the point <m>(10, 16)</m> means that there is a phrase with 20 letters in the English list, which corresponds to a phrase with 30 letters in the Tagalog list.</p>
      </solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-tagalog-graph-notice" workspace="1cm">
      <statement>
        <p>Just looking at the graph now, what do you notice about the relationship between the lengths of phrases in the two languages? (Compare to your previous answer.)</p>
      </statement>
    </exercise>

    </page>
    <page>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-tagalog-trend" workspace="1cm">
      <statement>
        <p>Draw a <q>trend</q> line to represent all points as best as you can. What's the use of this line? Discuss it!</p>
      </statement>
      <solution>
        <image source="palabras-tagalog-graph-sol.png" width="100%">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    
    <exercise xml:id="ex-tagalog-scaling" workspace="1cm">
      <statement>
        <p>What is a <em>reasonable</em> <term>scaling factor</term> from ENG to TAG?</p>
      </statement>
      <solution>
        <p>1.3 or similar. It's the slope of the trend line!</p>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
  </page>
  
</worksheet>
